  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>(1)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>Ni</mi><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;does not show isomerism because it is tetrahedral and&nbsp;has a&nbsp;plane of symmetry.</p><p>(2)<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Ni</mi><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msub><msub><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>shows geometrical isomerism.</p><p>(3)<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Ni</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>en</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> , shows optical isomerism.<br />(4)<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Pt</mi><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math> shows&nbsp;geometrical isomerism.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
